
# LocalCore — Product Blueprint (v0.2)

Windows desktop AI companion. Local-first, offline-capable, cloud optional and off by default.
Fully standalone — no CREAO-hosted services required. Extends the existing Electron project.

---

## 0. Locked decisions

| # | Decision | Choice | Consequence |
|---|---|---|---|
| D1 | Memory default | **Opt-out** — remembers by default, user can disable | Safety moves from consent-gating to transparency + one-click control (see §2) |
| D2 | Companion model | **One companion now**, multi-character-ready schema | Schema carries a `characterId`; UI shows one |
| D3 | Voice input | **Push-to-talk default**, wake word opt-in | Wake word must be on-device, explicit, and visibly indicated |
| D4 | Cloud posture | **Optional, off by default** | Enforced at the Egress Gateway, not by UI copy |
| D5 | Hosting | **None — fully standalone** | No CREAO services; cloud = third-party providers only |
| D6 | Hardware floor | **Integrated GPU / 8GB RAM, small models** | Drives model class, a resource governor, and realistic latency targets (see §1) |

### Invariants that survive all six decisions
- No network egress without an explicit, recorded consent event.
- All conversation, memory, and avatar data stays on device by default.
- The model is replaceable and addressed only through the Model Provider contract.
- Generated media is user data with inspect / save / delete controls.

