## 1. Hardware floor: what 8GB + integrated GPU actually implies

This is the binding constraint on the whole product. Designing for it up front avoids a rewrite.

**Model class**
- 1–3B parameter instruct models, Q4/Q5 quantized, CPU inference with optional integrated-GPU offload.
- Context window kept modest (small models degrade and slow down as context grows).
- Expect weaker instruction-following than cloud models — persona consistency and memory extraction must be engineered around it, not assumed.

**Resource governor (new, mandatory)**
Running the LLM, the VRM avatar, STT, and TTS at once does not fit in 8GB. One heavy pipeline at a time:
- Unload/evict the LLM when idle beyond a threshold; reload on next turn.
- Suspend avatar animation while a model loads; resume after.
- Serialize voice and generation — never run STT and LLM inference concurrently on the low tier.
- A tier detector picks quality presets (avatar fps/resolution, model size) from available RAM/VRAM.

**Realistic latency targets (to be measured, not promised)**
- First token: target under a few seconds on the floor machine; report actuals per hardware tier.
- Full response: streaming must start early so perceived latency is dominated by first token.
- Voice round-trip: noticeably slower than cloud; set expectations in the UI.

**Avatar budget**
- Cap ~30fps, simplified shaders, no post-processing on the low tier.
- Degrade: drop idle animation before dropping lip-sync; drop lip-sync before dropping chat.

