## 4. Component architecture (unchanged core, governor added)

- **Presentation** — chat, avatar window, tray, settings, permission dialogs.
- **Companion Core (Orchestrator)** — owns a turn end-to-end.
- **Capability services** — Model Provider, Memory, Voice, Avatar, Desktop Tools. No service calls another directly.
- **Platform services** — Permission & Consent, Egress Gateway, Asset Vault, Audit Log, **Resource Governor**.
- **Foundation** — Electron main/renderer, local storage, OS keychain/DPAPI.

Invariants: single egress choke point; services communicate only through the Orchestrator; every capability declares its requirements; the model is replaceable.

Contracts: Model Provider (stream + embeddings + capabilities descriptor), Memory (write/retrieve/list/edit/delete/export/wipe + per-category enable), Voice (transcribe / synthesize with viseme timing), Avatar (setEmotion/setPose/speakWithVisemes/setIdleProfile/setWindowMode), Desktop Tools (declare scope, dry-run description, approval, execute, log), Permission & Consent (request/grant/revoke, immediate effect), Egress Gateway (send + justification, deny-by-default), Resource Governor (acquire/release pipelines, evict idle).

Turn flow: input → memory check + retrieval → prompt assembly → streamed generation → avatar cues + optional TTS → persist → memory write (unless disabled) → audit.

