## 6. Standalone vs CREAO-hosted

**Decision D5: fully standalone. Nothing requires CREAO.**

| Capability | Where it runs |
|---|---|
| Chat, memory, voice, avatar, desktop tools, permissions, asset vault | Local Electron app |
| Model weights & VRM assets | Bundled or user-downloaded; no CREAO distribution |
| Optional cloud inference | Third-party provider, gated by Egress Gateway |
| Account sync / marketplace | **Not offered** — no server dependency |

The entire product, Phases 0–6, can ship with no server component. Any future hosted feature would be additive and must degrade to local-only.

---

## 7. Risks (re-ranked for the locked decisions)

1. **Low hardware floor (top risk).** 8GB + integrated GPU may not run LLM + avatar + voice concurrently. Mitigation: resource governor, serialization, quality tiers. This must be prototyped in Phase 0, not assumed.
2. **Weak small-model behavior.** Persona consistency and memory extraction will be rough at 1–3B. Mitigation: constrained extraction, structured memory formats, good persona engineering.
3. **Opt-out memory reputation.** Remembering by default is a trust risk if users feel surprised. Mitigation: first-run disclosure, permanent indicator, one-click wipe.
4. **Wake word privacy.** Always-listening invites scrutiny. Mitigation: off by default, on-device, visible armed indicator.
5. **Prompt injection via tools/retrieved content.** Treat all retrieved/tool content as untrusted data.
6. **Model licensing.** Ship license metadata with every bundled/downloadable model.
7. **Scope creep into OS automation.** Keep Phase 5 scoped and permissioned.

